  "articleBody": "It's tempting to tackle an interior framing project yourself, and for some small, non-structural jobs, it's totally doable. But there are definitely times when bringing in a qualified professional isn't just a good idea, it's essential for safety and compliance. For starters, if there's any chance the wall you're working on, or want to add, might be load-bearing, stop right there and call an expert. These walls are critical to your home's integrity, and you don't want to mess with them. Also, if you're creating new openings, like for a door or a pass-through, those need to be framed correctly with the right headers and support. An uneven floor or ceiling can also make framing tricky, and a pro knows how to adapt the framing to make everything look seamless. Plus, don't forget about permits and inspections. Many interior wall projects, even non-load-bearing ones, require them depending on your local rules here in the Denver area. A professional framer will know these requirements and ensure your project meets all code standards. At HH Remodeling, we can handle everything from verifying layout accuracy to ensuring your walls are perfectly plumb and ready for the next steps, taking the guesswork and stress out of your project.",
  "datePublished": "2026-08-09"
}